      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The retrieved evidence directly addresses the question. The Discussion section states that character n-grams are among the most effective features for addressing obfuscation, that many researchers have relied on text-based features, and that user profiling features (personal/community-based) significantly enhance state-of-the-art detection. The Neural-network section further reports that character n-grams contributed more than other features due to robustness to noise, and that character-level features were superior to word-level ones. Together these chunks provide insight into features commonly found predictive of abusive content, so the evidence fully supports an affirmative answer."
      },
